# Node / frontend tooling
node_modules/
dist/
build/
# .cache/ holds the §4 SKIP CACHE, and it is the entire reason a second full run
# costs 0.0s. Written by scripts/check_all.mjs, ~12 KB: one content hash per
# checker over the files it declared in `inputs`, plus the previous green run's
# duration and timestamp. Deleting it is safe and costs nothing but one slow run —
# every checker just re-runs once and writes it back — so it is ignored rather
# than defended. `.cache/recorded-inputs.json` is written only by --prove-inputs
# and is what proves the manifest's input lists against what the checkers
# actually read. The harness scratch directories that land under .cache/ are
# per-case temp trees, not state; deleting a stale one is harmless. See §4.
.cache/
.vite/

# Local environment and secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.local

