*.log
*.tmp
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# AGENTS.md.bak is a manually-made copy of AGENTS.md. It is not on disk right now
# — one existed until 2026-10-10 and was byte-identical to the live file, so it was
# never the "predecessor" this rule was written for, and it was deleted rather than
# left to rot. The rule stays because anyone who takes a backup copy must not have
# it swept into an unrelated commit by `git add -A`, which §6 forbids anyway. The
# *.json.bak rule above covers pokemon_data.json.bak; this one is separate because a
# markdown copy and a data backup are not the same kind of file.
AGENTS.md.bak

# Agent tooling state (.opencode/plans/*.md are session scratch, not project
# artifacts; .opencode/.gitignore already covers node_modules and package.json)
.opencode/

# .impeccable/ holds one dated UI critique per page the impeccable skill reviewed
# (.impeccable/critique/<timestamp>__<page>.md). Same category as .opencode/
# above: a tool's notes to itself, not something the repo consumes or a teammate
# would read. Not to be confused with docs/, which IS tracked — docs/incidents/
# is §3's record and docs/missing-pages.md is a planning artifact.
.impeccable/

# IDE settings
# The whole directory, not a whitelist of shared files. This repo is published, and
# .vscode/ is where editor state ends up (tasks the author never meant to share,
# launch configs with absolute paths, an extensions.json recommending the author's
# toolchain). The one file that looked like a project artifact was settings.json,
# pinning liveServer.settings.port to 5500 — but that port is Live Server's own
# default, so nothing is actually lost by not tracking it, and CRY_PORT exists for
# anyone running on a different port. Ignoring the directory leaves settings.json
# working exactly as before; it just stops being shared.
.idea/
.vscode/

# OS-generated files
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# *.json.bak is add_collection_tags.py's own pre-write backup, not an input.
*.json.bak

# Cloudflare Workers docs · Configuration and Bindings
# .assetsignore

# pokeapi_evolution_chains.json is the 541-chain cache behind
# assets/data/evolution_levels.json. 473 KB of a third-party API's JSON that
# changes whenever PokeAPI ships a change, and which fetch_evolution_levels.py
# rebuilds offline from -- or refetches with --refresh. Same rule as the
# InfoPoke captures above: the JSON the script PRODUCES is tracked, the raw
# response is not.
data-sources/pokeapi_evolution_chains.json

# pokeapi_form_stats.json is the 127-form cache behind the mega/gmax nodes in
# assets/data/graph_data.json, and the same rule applies: the JSON the script
# PRODUCES (graph_data.json, tracked) is in, the raw PokeAPI response is out, and
# fetch_form_stats.py rebuilds it with --refresh.
#
# The one difference from the file above is that build_graph_data.py reads this
# cache DIRECTLY rather than reading an assets/data/ table derived from it, so
# without it the form nodes fall back to the base species' types and stats --
# Charizard-Mega-X back to Fire/Flying -- rather than failing. That is why
# build_graph_data.py prints a WARNING naming the file and why
# check_graph_chip_network.mjs refuses to run without it, rather than ENOENTing.
# A fresh clone still has the correct graph, because graph_data.json is tracked.
data-sources/pokeapi_form_stats.json
